MASTER PROJECT CHARTER

Project Name:
Error: Not Found (working title)

Genre:
Roguelike deck-building card battler

Core Inspiration:
Slay the Spire style progression with cyberpunk narrative tone

Vision (What the game is)

A replayable, run-based card battler where the player progresses through a branching path, builds a deck dynamically, and engages in turn-based combat driven by synergy, randomness, and strategic planning.

The game emphasizes:

Clean, readable mechanics over clutter
Strong feedback loops (visual + mechanical)
High replayability through randomness and builds
A distinct cyberpunk identity layered over familiar systems
Non-Negotiables (What must remain true)
Turn-based combat only (no real-time mechanics)
Card-driven actions (no separate ability system outside cards)
Deterministic rules with controlled randomness (no chaos systems)
Modular systems (map, combat, cards, enemies must be separable)
No system rewrites once interfaces are established
What the game is NOT
Not an RPG with free movement
Not an action game
Not reliant on heavy story to function
Not dependent on external APIs or online systems
Core Gameplay Loop
Player selects next node on a branching map
Enters encounter (combat/event/shop)
Executes turn-based card combat
Receives rewards (cards, relics, upgrades)
Modifies deck
Repeats until death or completion
Primary Systems
Map / Path Generation
Card Engine (draw, play, discard, exhaust)
Combat State Machine
Enemy Intent System
Reward + Deck Building System
Animation + Visual Feedback Layer
Audio System
Save / Load System
Design Pillars
Every card must feel meaningful
Every run must feel different
UI clarity > visual complexity
Systems must be testable without visuals
No hidden mechanics (player can learn everything)